An update on this @participant7: I verified and it is using the latest version. 

When my app is in the foreground, I get a notificationd and click on it, I see the ["response received" log](https://github.com/expo/expo/blob/d6515f12fc9eee6d563cc4de32f9aee5c856158f/packages/expo-notifications/build/NotificationsEmitter.js#L87) and everything works fine. However, when my app is closed (fully), I get a notification and click on it to open the app, then I don't see that "response received" log, the "data" field is missing and the request content contains the "dataString" field.

Looking at the code for `useLastNotificationResponse`, I believe this happens because in the first scenario, the notification comes from the [response received listener](https://github.com/expo/expo/blob/d6515f12fc9eee6d563cc4de32f9aee5c856158f/packages/expo-notifications/build/useLastNotificationResponse.js#L45), which does parse the "dataString" (that's the change from the link you sent me). In the second scenario though, the notification seems to be coming from [getLastNotificationResponseAsync](https://github.com/expo/expo/blob/d6515f12fc9eee6d563cc4de32f9aee5c856158f/packages/expo-notifications/build/useLastNotificationResponse.js#L59) which does not parse the "dataString".

