@participant7 `expo-notifications 0.28.8` will work for people using the nodejs server SDK, however it is not working with the [PHP Expo Server SDK](https://github.com/ctwillie/expo-server-sdk-php) nor the [expo testing tool](https://expo.dev/notifications) for the **first background notification** sent on Android. Other SDKs might be affected. 

Full explanation & patch for `onNotificationResponseFromExtras()` are in this comment: https://github.com/expo/expo/issues/28656#issuecomment-2155676511 .  Here's the important bit:


1. Open app > background it
2. Send a fcmv1 notification using the expo tool: https://expo.dev/notifications (or the [PHP Expo Server SDK](https://github.com/ctwillie/expo-server-sdk-php) )
3. Tap the notification

result: notification not received in the client.

An important thing to note here is this bug doesn't repro using the `nodejs expo-server-sdk@3.9.0`. When using that SDK, this notification comes in unmarshaled via `ExpoNotificationLifecycleListener.onNewIntent()` (which is skipped) but is then picked up by the listeners in the `NotificationManager`.

However, when using the expo tool or the php implementation, it comes through as a valid notification, but it is not picked up by the listeners. Instead, it is passed through to `ExpoNotificationLifecycleListener.onNewIntent()` and then to `onNotificationResponseFromExtras()`. However, there's a bug with that method - it doesn't process notifications if the listeners have already been setup, which in this case they have. 

Here is the patch to fix this issue:
```java
// old

 public void onNotificationResponseFromExtras(Bundle extras) {
   // bug exists here - if we have listeners already setup and 
   // we're processing a notification from a background state
   // this notification will be added to mPendingNotificationResponsesFromExtras 
   // and never gets processed
    if (mPendingNotificationResponsesFromExtras.isEmpty()) {
      mPendingNotificationResponsesFromExtras.add(extras);
    } else {
      for (WeakReference<NotificationListener> listenerReference : mListenerReferenceMap.values()) {
        NotificationListener listener = listenerReference.get();
        if (listener != null) {
          listener.onNotificationResponseIntentReceived(extras);
        }
      }
    }
  }

// patched

 public void onNotificationResponseFromExtras(Bundle extras) {
    // We're going to be passed in extras from either
    // a killed state (ExpoNotificationLifecycleListener::onCreate)
    // OR a background state (ExpoNotificationLifecycleListener::onNewIntent)

    // If we've just come from a background state, we'll have listeners set up
    // pass on the notification to them
    if (!mListenerReferenceMap.isEmpty()) {
      for (WeakReference<NotificationListener> listenerReference : mListenerReferenceMap.values()) {
        NotificationListener listener = listenerReference.get();
        if (listener != null) {
          listener.onNotificationResponseIntentReceived(extras);
        }
      }
    } else {
      // Otherwise, the app has been launched from a killed state, and our listeners
      // haven't yet been setup. We'll add this to a list of pending notifications
      // for them to process once they've been initialized.
      if (mPendingNotificationResponsesFromExtras.isEmpty()) {
        mPendingNotificationResponsesFromExtras.add(extras);
      }
    }
  }
```

